North Korea says it won't be disarmament undiminished without confidence
North Korea's Foreign Minister told the United Nations on Saturday that the ongoing sanctions are deepening a sense of disbeliech towards the U.S. and that his country was not going to unilaterally abandon its nuclear weapons under such circumstances.
Yong Kho told the global organization's annual general assembly that North Korea had taken "important good-volunteering measures" in the past year, e.g. the interruption of nuclear and ballistic tests, dismantling the nuclear test facilities and the freezing non-proliferation of nuclear weapons and nuclear technology.
"However, we don''t see any corresponding response from the United States," he said.
