Software problems were particularly significant; as Baden-Wuerttemberg class ships have a crew of around 120 seafarers, just a half compared to older Bremen-class frigates.
It was also disclosed that the ship has a much greater weight, which reduces its performance and limits the Navy's ability to add future upgrades.
